===Etymology===
From the variant {{m|it|ciriegia}}, from {{inh|it|VL.|ceresia}}, from the neuter plural of {{der|it|LL.|ceresium}}, from {{der|it|la|cerasium}}, from {{der|it|grc|κεράσιον||cherry}}, from {{m|grc|κερασός||[[bird cherry]]}}, ultimately possibly of {{der|it|ine-ana|-}} origin. Alternatively from {{m|it|ciliegio}}, {{m|it|ciriegio}} (Tuscan), from {{der|it|LL.|ceresus}}, from {{der|it|la|cerasus}}. See also {{m|it|cerasa}}.

